{"call_id":"e419b6ff591e1b8c","request_hash":"01aadff1ac031db7457ad51332ddd02a18e61b318759d8bf193c7fcf85a3a5c4","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"SHARED-000","condition":"baseline"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"01aadff1ac031db7457ad51332ddd02a18e61b318759d8bf193c7fcf85a3a5c4","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"If your Halvard Home Keel washing machine vibrates more than usual:\n\n1. **Pause the programme and wait for the drum to stop.**\n2. If the door unlocks, spread heavy items, such as towels, evenly around the drum, then restart the programme. **Do not force the door open.**\n3. Check that the machine stands firmly on a hard, level floor. All four feet should touch the floor, and it should not rock when gently pushed at opposite corners. Switch it off and unplug it before adjusting the feet.\n4. If it is newly installed, check the installation guide to confirm that all transit bolts were removed.\n\nIf strong vibration continues, **stop using the machine and contact Halvard Home support.**","input_tokens":829,"output_tokens":154,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1330.4500998929143,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":3551.3410000130534,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:22.287623+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:22.298443+00:00"}
