{"call_id":"d3fef2b16410ce92","request_hash":"2d2e629c77d1c8bf85bc3f469e78a08975215e39cc103110d3a8498f2831a174","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"TWOPART-001","condition":"baseline"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"2d2e629c77d1c8bf85bc3f469e78a08975215e39cc103110d3a8498f2831a174","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"In Wales and West, a warranty engineer visit is **offered within 46 hours** of your claim being accepted; this does not guarantee the repair will be completed during that visit. [P5]\n\nThe passages do **not specify a routine service price** for the Brio kettle. They list **£79 for a Brio engineer visit after the warranty ends** [P1] and **£70 for a general Wales and West call-out**, covering attendance and assessment, with repair costs separate. [P3]","input_tokens":1368,"output_tokens":109,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1278.2546998932958,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":2912.1121000498533,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:23.149339+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:23.170576+00:00"}
{"call_id":"eb1988282ff7585c","request_hash":"90c156e43067350e391cb1d486cf987df95df3d7a90d9410739b9255d997dc20","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"VERSION-000","condition":"baseline"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"90c156e43067350e391cb1d486cf987df95df3d7a90d9410739b9255d997dc20","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"The passages give conflicting cooling times: **11 minutes in P1** and **7 minutes in P2**. To be cautious, wait **at least 11 minutes**, and longer if the surfaces are still too hot to touch safely.","input_tokens":1245,"output_tokens":52,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":2157.835000194609,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":3056.583800120279,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:23.795591+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:23.847895+00:00"}
{"call_id":"e96b33c1ae4faa1b","request_hash":"95beb8fe8b0d8e111754242c37baf90473e0f661020e3f4788fa07cd8dd6fe7e","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"VERSION-001","condition":"baseline"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"95beb8fe8b0d8e111754242c37baf90473e0f661020e3f4788fa07cd8dd6fe7e","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"The passages conflict: **P1 says to wait 45 hours**, while **P2 says 4 hours** after moving it. Confirm the correct waiting period with Halvard Home before switching it on. If the thermostat is damaged or has been exposed to water, leave it disconnected regardless of how long you’ve waited.","input_tokens":1150,"output_tokens":68,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":1379.85650007613,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":3047.5630001164973,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:24.456256+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:24.472195+00:00"}
{"call_id":"7a7842ceb1d14cca","request_hash":"2446b6f18c66107bd062ccb91d4e48f1df7dbf9fe745d717b2f10f4e13443e68","model_label":"gpt-6.1-sol","mode":"answer","cell":{"item":"SHARED-001","condition":"baseline"},"source":"api","attempts":1,"result":{"request_hash":"2446b6f18c66107bd062ccb91d4e48f1df7dbf9fe745d717b2f10f4e13443e68","provider":"openai","model_requested":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_returned":"gpt-6.1-sol","text":"If water is leaking underneath your Keel washing machine:\n\n1. **Stop the cycle and turn off the water supply tap.** Switch off and unplug the machine only if the plug and surrounding area are dry and safe to reach. Do not touch a wet socket or plug.\n2. Once safe, wipe up the water and check, **without moving the machine**, for:\n   - Drips at visible inlet hose connections.\n   - A drain hose that has slipped out of its drain.\n   - Water running down from the detergent drawer—too much detergent can cause excess foam and leaks.\n3. **Do not run another cycle while the leak remains unexplained.** If the hoses appear secure or water is coming from beneath the casing, contact Halvard Home support to arrange an engineer inspection. Do not remove panels or try to seal the leak yourself.\n\nHave your machine’s serial number and purchase details ready, and describe where and when the water appears. If it is within the two-year warranty, ask for a warranty assessment; manufacturing faults may be covered. [P1, P2, P5]","input_tokens":830,"output_tokens":226,"reasoning_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"time_to_first_answer_token_ms":2260.435299947858,"time_to_first_thinking_ms":null,"total_latency_ms":5318.692000117153,"finish_reason":"stop","timestamp_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:24.556361+00:00","error":null},"error":null,"recorded_utc":"2026-10-12T15:35:24.571540+00:00"}
